WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.280
Imagine you find an old photograph of a clay pot.

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.012
You’d love to put it in a digital exhibition.

00:00:06.012 --> 00:00:07.751
Where did the photo come from?

00:00:07.751 --> 00:00:09.207
Whose story does it tell?

00:00:09.657 --> 00:00:11.552
Find out who can give permission.

00:00:11.552 --> 00:00:13.259
Can the image go online?

00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:14.134
For how long?

00:00:14.134 --> 00:00:15.731
And can you make changes to it?

00:00:16.051 --> 00:00:18.558
Keep a record of the source and the credit.

00:00:18.558 --> 00:00:20.992
If part of the image is reconstructed,

00:00:20.992 --> 00:00:23.534
mark it so visitors can see what was added.

00:00:23.894 --> 00:00:25.845
Try a single sample first.

00:00:25.845 --> 00:00:28.189
Show it to someone who knows the history.

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:29.914
Does the story ring true?

00:00:29.914 --> 00:00:31.852
Is this the right way to tell it?

00:00:32.352 --> 00:00:34.378
Then talk about who’ll look after it,

00:00:34.378 --> 00:00:37.497
and how any income could help conserve the original.

00:00:37.497 --> 00:00:41.139
Use the partnership link below to tell us about your project.
